    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of ha degraded land and highly disturbed remnant of natural forest land restored and conserved.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">750 ha of land is covered with natural vegetation/forest and woodland.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifting the project out of the suspension mode and start implementation</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the project has been stalled for several years, review of the Project Document is under way is currently at advanced stage. Expected date for completion of the review process is January 2023. The purpose of the review is to determine whether the project rationale/logic, expected results (Outcome, Outputs, and activities), and budget against cost items are still relevant. And where it deems necessary and appropriate, amendments/adjustments shall be done accordingly. Moreover, the exercise will be instrumental to look into and assess implementation or execution arrangements and to propose appropriate and adequate ones to facilitate resumption of implementation.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the CEO endorsement of the Rora Habab project (PIMS 5519) in June 2018, the project has remained stalled,. CO jointly with the IP (Ministry of Land, Water and Environment) are working to revitalize the project for implementation.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">NA</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the CEO endorsement of the Rora Habab project (PIMS 5519) in June 2018, the Government of Eritrea has not been able to initiate implementation of these two projects due to various institutional challenges.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the CEO endorsement of the Rora Habab project (PIMS 5519) in June 2018, the Government of Eritrea has not been able to initiate implementation of these two projects due to various institutional challenges. 
In the face of these challenges and to avoid the risk of cancellation of the projects, in May 2021, UNDP CO and the government agreed, in line with GEF rules and procedures, to suspend the projects to allow for appropriate arrangements to be put in place to facilitate initiation of project implementation activities. Based on the agreement reached between the UNDP CO and the Ministry of Land, Water and Environment of the government of the state of Eritrea, the project is under suspension.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
